        "segmentId": "m00355:caption:fig-00002-caption"
      },
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00355:alt:fig-00002-alt",
          "text": "Initiation involves two steps and propagation involves four steps. Olefin reacts with Grubbs catalyst forming metallacycle. It further gives another catalyst form, that reacts with olefin 2 to form product."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_31_05_002.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00003",
      "segmentId": "m00355:para:para-00003"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00003",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00355:alt:fig-00003-alt",
          "text": "Cyclopentene reacts with Grubbs catalyst to form the first intermediate which reacts to form second intermediate. This reacts with the catalyst to form a third intermediate leading to a polymer."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_31_05_003.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00004",
      "segmentId": "m00355:para:para-00004"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00004",
      "class": "unnumbered",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00355:alt:fig-00004-alt",
          "text": "Two molecules of 1,8-nonadiene react with a catalyst to create an intermediate and ethylene molecule. Further cycles generate a polymer of n units and n moles of ethylene molecule."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_31_05_004.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00005",
